<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Way of the Five Pecks of Rice</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Five Pecks of Rice, Celestial Masters</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Way of the Five Pecks of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">Rice</a> was an early Daoist religious movement founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sichuan">Sichuan</a> in the second century CE by Zhang Daoling, named after the contribution of rice paid by its members. Under his grandson Zhang Lu it ran a theocratic state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanzhong">Hanzhong</a> until 215. It developed into the Way of the Celestial Masters, the first organised Daoist church, which spread across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and inspired the rebellion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sun-en">Sun En</a> in 399.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/way-of-the-five-pecks-of-rice.jpg" alt="Way of the Five Pecks of Rice" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charlie fong · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hanzhong_baoheriver.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
